# agy hook payloads, shell of run_command, empty hook stdout, two stdin turns (ADR-0086 D2/D9/D12; #784 Stage 1, 2026-11-12).
# Windows 11, agy 1.5.6, isolated root --gemini_dir=<tmp>\gd (auth from the Windows keyring), model gemini-3.8-flash-low,
# --input-format stream-json --output-format stream-json --dangerously-skip-permissions. Paths: <home> = %USERPROFILE%.
# Recorder: <python> -I rec.py <PreToolUse reply> <other reply> <dir>; it saves each stdin payload whole, then replies.
# hooks.json (agy format: top-level key = hook name; tool events wrap handlers in {matcher, hooks:[..]}, others are flat):
#   {"ralphy-probe":{"SessionStart":[{"type":"command","command":"<cmd>"}],"PreToolUse":[{"matcher":"*","hooks":[{"type":"command","command":"<cmd>"}]}], ...}}
# A first attempt wrapped the events in a top-level "hooks" key: agy logged 'invalid hook "hooks": command hook must specify command' and ran none.
# Tool names in the stream and payloads: run_command, write_file, edit_file, read_file. The init tool list also names write_to_file,
# replace_file_content, multi_replace_file_content, sed_file, notebook_edit; asked to use them by name (probe P5), the model answered
# that only write_file and edit_file are available to it, and no PreToolUse fired.
# Init tool list elided below as [...].

## P1 payloads: PreToolUse prints {"decision":"allow"}, other events print {}
prompt: run `echo probe`; create a.txt (one,two,three); edit line two with the edit tool; read a.txt.
Hook order (rec_p1 events.log): SessionStart, then per model call PreInvocation, [PreToolUse, PostToolUse], PostInvocation; last PreInvocation, PostInvocation, Stop.
Tools called, with toolCall.args shape: run_command {CommandLine,WaitMsBeforeAsync,toolSummary}; write_file {Path,Content}; edit_file {Path,Target,Replacement}; read_file {Path}.
toolCall = {args, id, name}; stepIdx on PreToolUse and PostToolUse; PostToolUse adds error; Stop adds terminationReason,fullyIdle,continuationActive,executionNum,error.
Paths inside payloads: workspacePaths and transcriptPath use forward slashes; cwd and args.Path use backslashes. a.txt ended 'one
TWO
three
'.
Payload files are in crates/ralphy-cli/tests/fixtures/antigravity-hooks/.
